IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`

-- The Convention, Chapter III: liability of the carrier (Articles 17 to 30A).
-- Source: source/CAA1988.txt lines 505 to 690 (First Schedule), 1114 to 1267 (Second Schedule)
-- and 1665 to 1911 (Third Schedule).
--
-- Every rule that differs between the three texts takes the Convention as its first input.
-- The sums in francs and Special Drawing Rights are limits in those units; converting them
-- to Singapore dollars is for the Minister's order under s 6(4) of the Act (caa-act.l4).

§ `Chapter III -- Liability of the carrier`

§§ `Article 17. Death or injury of a passenger`

@ref "Convention, Article 17"
GIVEN p IS A `Passenger Accident Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable under Article 17` IF
        p's `the damage is death, wounding or other bodily injury suffered by a passenger`
    AND (   p's `the accident which caused the damage took place on board the aircraft`
         OR p's `the accident took place in the course of any of the operations of embarking or disembarking`)

§§ `Article 18. Destruction, loss of or damage to baggage or cargo`

-- 18(3) (First and Second: 18(3); Third: 18(5)): carriage by land, sea or river outside an
-- aerodrome is outside the carriage by air, but if it takes place in the performance of a
-- contract for carriage by air, for loading, delivery or transhipment, any damage is presumed,
-- subject to proof to the contrary, to have resulted from an event during the carriage by air.

@ref "Convention, Article 18(3) (First and Second Schedules) and Article 18(5) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN f IS A `Cargo Loss Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damage is presumed to have resulted from an event during the carriage by air` IF
        f's `the occurrence took place in carriage by land, sea or river performed outside an aerodrome or airport`
    AND f's `that carriage took place in the performance of a contract for carriage by air, for the purpose of loading, delivery or transhipment`
    AND NOT f's `there is proof to the contrary`

@ref "Convention, Article 18(2) and (3) (First and Second Schedules) and Article 18(4) and (5) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN f IS A `Cargo Loss Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occurrence is within the carriage by air` IF
        f's `the occurrence which caused the damage took place during the carriage by air`
     OR f's `the baggage or cargo was in the charge of the carrier in an aerodrome or airport, on board an aircraft, or in any place after a landing outside an aerodrome`
     OR `the damage is presumed to have resulted from an event during the carriage by air` f

-- 18(1): First and Second Schedules: baggage or cargo, if the occurrence was during the
-- carriage by air.  Third Schedule: baggage on the same footing (18(1)); cargo "upon condition
-- only" that the occurrence was during the carriage by air (18(2)), and not if the carrier
-- proves the loss resulted solely from an inherent defect, defective packaging by another,
-- an act of war or armed conflict, or an act of public authority (18(3)).

@ref "Convention, Article 18(1) to (3) (Third Schedule) and Article 18(1) (First and Second Schedules)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Cargo Loss Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable under Article 18` IF
        (   f's `the damage is destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage`
         OR f's `the damage is destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo`)
    AND `the occurrence is within the carriage by air` f
    AND (CONSIDER c
         WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
             (IF f's `the damage is destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo`
              THEN NOT (   f's `the carrier proves that the loss or damage resulted solely from an inherent defect, quality or vice of the cargo`
                        OR f's `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from defective packaging of the cargo by a person other than the carrier or his servants or agents`
                        OR f's `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from an act of war or an armed conflict`
                        OR f's `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from an act of public authority carried out in connexion with the entry, exit or transit of the cargo`)
              ELSE TRUE))

§§ `Article 19. Delay`

@ref "Convention, Article 19"
GIVEN `the damage is occasioned by delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable under Article 19` IF
    `the damage is occasioned by delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo`

§§ `Article 20. Defence`

-- 20 (Second Schedule): the carrier is not liable if he proves that he and his servants and
-- agents took all necessary measures, or that it was impossible; and, in the carriage of cargo
-- and baggage, that the damage was occasioned by negligent pilotage or in handling the
-- aircraft or navigation and that in all other respects he and his agents took all necessary
-- measures.  20 (First Schedule): the first defence only.  20 (Third Schedule): the first
-- defence, in the carriage of passengers and baggage and for damage occasioned by delay in the
-- carriage of cargo; not for destruction, loss or damage of cargo (Article 18(3) applies).

@ref "Convention, Article 20"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      g IS A `Ground of Liability`
      d IS A `Defence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
            d's `the carrier proves that he and his servants and agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage`
         OR d's `the carrier proves that it was impossible for him and them to take such measures`
         OR (    (CONSIDER g
                  WHEN `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage` THEN TRUE
                  WHEN `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` THEN TRUE
                  OTHERWISE FALSE)
             AND d's `the carrier proves that the damage was occasioned by negligent pilotage or negligence in the handling of the aircraft or in navigation`
             AND d's `the carrier proves that in all other respects he and his agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage`)
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            d's `the carrier proves that he and his servants and agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage`
         OR d's `the carrier proves that it was impossible for him and them to take such measures`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            (CONSIDER g
             WHEN `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` THEN FALSE
             OTHERWISE TRUE)
        AND (   d's `the carrier proves that he and his servants and agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage`
             OR d's `the carrier proves that it was impossible for him and them to take such measures`)

§§ `Article 21. Contributory negligence`

-- 21: if the carrier proves the damage was caused or contributed to by the negligence of the
-- injured person, the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly, in accordance with its
-- own law (First and Second Schedules; Third Schedule for passengers and baggage).  Third
-- Schedule, cargo: the carrier "shall be wholly or partly exonerated" to the extent the
-- claimant's negligence or wrongful act caused or contributed to the damage.

@ref "Convention, Article 21"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
      n IS A `Contributory Negligence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN n's `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the person suffering the damage`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN n's `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the person suffering the damage`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        (CONSIDER k
         WHEN `cargo` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE n's `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the person suffering the damage`)

@ref "Convention, Article 21(2) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
      n IS A `Contributory Negligence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        (CONSIDER k
         WHEN `cargo` THEN n's `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence or other wrongful act or omission of the person claiming compensation or the person from whom he derives his rights`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `Article 22. Limits of liability`

-- 22(1): passengers: 125,000 francs (Second Schedule); 250,000 francs (First and Third).
-- 22(2): registered baggage and cargo: 250 francs per kilogramme (First and Second); registered
-- baggage 250 francs per kilogramme and cargo 17 Special Drawing Rights per kilogramme (Third).
-- 22(3): objects the passenger takes charge of himself: 5,000 francs per passenger.

@ref "Convention, Article 22(1), (2) and (3)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Limit`
GIVETH A `Liability Limit`
`the liability limit under Article 22` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 125_000, Francs, FALSE
        WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 250_000, Francs, FALSE
        WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 250_000, Francs, FALSE
    WHEN `the liability for registered baggage` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 250, Francs, TRUE
    WHEN `the liability for cargo` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 250, Francs, TRUE
        WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 250, Francs, TRUE
        WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 17, `Special Drawing Rights`, TRUE
    WHEN `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself` THEN `Liability Limit` OF 5_000, Francs, FALSE

-- 22(2)(b) and (c) (First and Third): where part of registered baggage or cargo, or an object
-- in it, is lost, damaged or delayed, the weight taken into account is only the weight of the
-- package or packages concerned; but where that affects the value of other packages covered by
-- the same baggage check or air waybill, their weight is also taken into account.  The Second
-- Schedule has no such rule.

@ref "Convention, Article 22(2)(b) (First Schedule) and Article 22(2)(c) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      l IS A `Limit Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weight taken into consideration in determining the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        IF l's `the loss, damage or delay of part affects the value of other packages covered by the same baggage check or air waybill`
        THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) states no rule for the weight to be taken into consideration where the loss, damage or delay of part affects other packages"
        ELSE l's `the total weight in kilogrammes of the package or packages concerned`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        l's `the total weight in kilogrammes of the package or packages concerned`
            PLUS (IF l's `the loss, damage or delay of part affects the value of other packages covered by the same baggage check or air waybill`
                  THEN l's `the total weight in kilogrammes of those other packages`
                  ELSE 0)
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        l's `the total weight in kilogrammes of the package or packages concerned`
            PLUS (IF l's `the loss, damage or delay of part affects the value of other packages covered by the same baggage check or air waybill`
                  THEN l's `the total weight in kilogrammes of those other packages`
                  ELSE 0)

-- The amount, in the unit of the limit.  Passengers: the limit, or a higher limit agreed by
-- special contract.  Baggage and cargo: the rate per kilogramme times the weight, unless the
-- passenger or consignor made a special declaration at handover and paid any supplementary
-- sum, in which case the carrier is liable up to the declared sum, unless he proves the
-- declared sum exceeds the actual interest in delivery, when the actual interest is the
-- measure.

@ref "Convention, Article 22(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Limit`
      l IS A `Limit Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` THEN
        IF l's `the passenger and the carrier have agreed by special contract a higher limit`
        THEN l's `the higher limit agreed`
        ELSE (`the liability limit under Article 22` c k)'s `the amount`
    WHEN `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself` THEN
        (`the liability limit under Article 22` c k)'s `the amount`
    WHEN `the liability for registered baggage` THEN
        IF l's `a special declaration of interest in delivery at destination was made at the time the package was handed over and any supplementary sum has been paid`
        THEN (IF l's `the carrier proves that the declared sum is greater than the actual interest in delivery at destination`
              THEN l's `the actual interest in delivery at destination`
              ELSE l's `the declared sum`)
        ELSE (`the liability limit under Article 22` c k)'s `the amount` TIMES `the weight taken into consideration in determining the limit` c l
    WHEN `the liability for cargo` THEN
        IF l's `a special declaration of interest in delivery at destination was made at the time the package was handed over and any supplementary sum has been paid`
        THEN (IF l's `the carrier proves that the declared sum is greater than the actual interest in delivery at destination`
              THEN l's `the actual interest in delivery at destination`
              ELSE l's `the declared sum`)
        ELSE (`the liability limit under Article 22` c k)'s `the amount` TIMES `the weight taken into consideration in determining the limit` c l

-- 22(4) (First and Third): the limits do not prevent the court awarding the whole or part of
-- the costs and other expenses of the litigation, unless the damages awarded, excluding costs,
-- do not exceed the sum the carrier offered in writing within 6 months from the occurrence, or
-- before the action began if that is later.  The Second Schedule's 22(4) is the definition of the
-- franc and has no such rule.

@ref "Convention, Article 22(4) (First and Third Schedules)"
GIVEN k IS A `Costs Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier's offer was made in time` IF
    CONSIDER k's `the date the carrier made the offer, if it was made`
    WHEN JUST offered THEN
            offered AT MOST `add months` (k's `the date of the occurrence causing the damage`) 6
         OR offered LESS THAN k's `the date the action was commenced`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref "Convention, Article 22(4) (First and Third Schedules)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Costs Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no rule on costs and other expenses of the litigation in Article 22"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        NOT (    `the carrier's offer was made in time` k
             AND (CONSIDER k's `the sum the carrier offered in writing to the plaintiff, if any`
                  WHEN JUST offer THEN k's `the amount of the damages awarded, excluding court costs and other expenses of the litigation` AT MOST offer
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        NOT (    `the carrier's offer was made in time` k
             AND (CONSIDER k's `the sum the carrier offered in writing to the plaintiff, if any`
                  WHEN JUST offer THEN k's `the amount of the damages awarded, excluding court costs and other expenses of the litigation` AT MOST offer
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))

-- 22(4) (Second), 22(5) (First and Third): the franc is a currency unit of 65.5 milligrammes
-- of gold of millesimal fineness 900; the sums may be converted into national currencies in
-- round figures.  22(6) (Third): Special Drawing Rights are as defined by the International
-- Monetary Fund and converted at the date of judgment; States that are not IMF members whose
-- law does not permit 22(2)(b) may declare a limit of 250 monetary units per kilogramme.
-- These are definitions and conversion rules; the conversion to Singapore dollars is the
-- Minister's under s 6(4) of the Act (caa-act.l4): inert here.

§§ `Article 23. Contractual provisions`

@ref "Convention, Article 23(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Clause Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is null and void under Article 23` IF
        k's `the clause tends to relieve the carrier of liability or to fix a lower limit than that laid down in the Convention`
    AND (CONSIDER c
         WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN NOT k's `the clause is a provision governing loss or damage resulting from the inherent defect, quality or vice of the cargo carried`
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN NOT k's `the clause is a provision governing loss or damage resulting from the inherent defect, quality or vice of the cargo carried`)

@ref "Convention, Article 23(1)"
`the nullity of such a provision involves the nullity of the whole contract of carriage` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Article 24. Exclusivity of the Convention's conditions and limits`

-- 24: in the cases covered by Articles 17, 18 and 19 any action for damages, however founded,
-- can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits set out in the Convention (First
-- and Second Schedules; Third Schedule for passengers and baggage, and for cargo whether in
-- contract, tort or otherwise), without prejudice to who may sue.  In the Third Schedule the
-- cargo limits are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances.

@ref "Convention, Article 24"
GIVEN g IS A `Ground of Liability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action for damages can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits of the Convention` IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo` THEN TRUE

@ref "Convention, Article 24(2) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the limits of liability are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) does not say that the limits are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) does not say that the limits are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        (CONSIDER k
         WHEN `cargo` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `Article 25. Loss of the benefit of the limits`

-- 25 (Second Schedule): the carrier is not entitled to the provisions excluding or limiting
-- liability if the damage is caused by his wilful misconduct, or by such default as the law of
-- the court seised of the case considers equivalent to wilful misconduct, or so caused by a
-- servant or agent acting within the scope of his employment.  25 (First and Third): the
-- limits do not apply if the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier, his
-- servants or agents, done with intent to cause damage or recklessly and with knowledge that
-- damage would probably result (for a servant or agent, also within the scope of employment);
-- in the Third Schedule that applies to passengers and baggage only.

@ref "Convention, Article 25"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
      b IS A `Limit Breaking Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the limits of liability apply` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        NOT (   b's `the damage is caused by the wilful misconduct of the carrier`
             OR b's `the damage is caused by such default of the carrier as, according to the law of the court seised of the case, is considered equivalent to wilful misconduct`
             OR b's `the damage is so caused by a servant or agent of the carrier acting within the scope of his employment`)
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        NOT (   b's `the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier done with intent to cause damage or recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result`
             OR (    b's `the damage resulted from such an act or omission of a servant or agent`
                 AND b's `the servant or agent was acting within the scope of his employment`))
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        (CONSIDER k
         WHEN `cargo` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE
            NOT (   b's `the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier done with intent to cause damage or recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result`
                 OR (    b's `the damage resulted from such an act or omission of a servant or agent`
                     AND b's `the servant or agent was acting within the scope of his employment`)))

§§ `Article 25A. Servants and agents`

-- 25A(1), (3): a servant or agent sued on damage to which the Convention relates who proves he
-- acted within the scope of his employment may avail himself of the carrier's Article 22
-- limits, unless the damage resulted from his act or omission done with intent or recklessly
-- and with knowledge that damage would probably result (Third Schedule: in the carriage of
-- passengers and baggage only).  25A(2): the aggregate recoverable from the carrier and his
-- servants and agents may not exceed the limits.  The Second Schedule has no Article 25A.

@ref "Convention, Article 25A(1) and (3)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
      s IS A `Servant Limit Facts`
      b IS A `Limit Breaking Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the servant or agent may avail himself of the limits of liability` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no Article 25A entitling a servant or agent to the carrier's limits"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            s's `an action is brought against a servant or agent of the carrier arising out of damage to which the Convention relates`
        AND s's `the servant or agent proves that he acted within the scope of his employment`
        AND NOT b's `the damage resulted from such an act or omission of a servant or agent`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            s's `an action is brought against a servant or agent of the carrier arising out of damage to which the Convention relates`
        AND s's `the servant or agent proves that he acted within the scope of his employment`
        AND (CONSIDER k
             WHEN `cargo` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOT b's `the damage resulted from such an act or omission of a servant or agent`)

@ref "Convention, Article 25A(2)"
GIVEN s IS A `Servant Limit Facts`
      `the limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aggregate recoverable from the carrier and his servants and agents is within the limit` IF
    s's `the amount recoverable from the carrier` PLUS s's `the amount recoverable from his servants and agents` AT MOST `the limit`

§§ `Article 26. Complaint`

-- 26(2): the person entitled to delivery must complain forthwith after the discovery of the
-- damage, and at the latest within 3 days (baggage) and 7 days (cargo) from receipt, and in
-- the case of delay 14 days from the date the baggage or cargo was placed at his disposal
-- (Second Schedule); 7, 14 and 21 days (First and Third Schedules).  "Days" means current
-- days (Article 35).

@ref "Convention, Article 26(2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      k IS A `Kind of Complaint`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days allowed for the complaint` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `damage to baggage` THEN 3
        WHEN `damage to cargo` THEN 7
        WHEN `delay of baggage` THEN 14
        WHEN `delay of cargo` THEN 14
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `damage to baggage` THEN 7
        WHEN `damage to cargo` THEN 14
        WHEN `delay of baggage` THEN 21
        WHEN `delay of cargo` THEN 21
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `damage to baggage` THEN 7
        WHEN `damage to cargo` THEN 14
        WHEN `delay of baggage` THEN 21
        WHEN `delay of cargo` THEN 21

@ref "Convention, Article 26(2) and Article 35"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Complaint Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the complaint` MEANS
    f's `the date of receipt, or the date the baggage or cargo was placed at the disposal of the person entitled to delivery`
        PLUS `the number of days allowed for the complaint` c (f's `kind of complaint`)

-- 26(2), (3): the complaint must be made within the time, forthwith after discovery where it
-- is damage, and in writing on the document of carriage or by separate notice despatched
-- within the times.

@ref "Convention, Article 26(2) and (3)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Complaint Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint was made in time` IF
        f's `the date the complaint was made` AT MOST `the last day for the complaint` c f
    AND (CONSIDER f's `kind of complaint`
         WHEN `damage to baggage` THEN f's `the complaint was made forthwith after the discovery of the damage`
         WHEN `damage to cargo` THEN f's `the complaint was made forthwith after the discovery of the damage`
         WHEN `delay of baggage` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `delay of cargo` THEN TRUE)
    AND f's `the complaint is in writing upon the document of carriage or by separate notice in writing despatched within the times`

@ref "Convention, Article 26(4)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Complaint Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action lies against the carrier` IF
        `the complaint was made in time` c f
     OR f's `the carrier was guilty of fraud`

@ref "Convention, Article 26(1)"
`receipt by the person entitled to delivery without complaint is prima facie evidence that the baggage or cargo was delivered in good condition and in accordance with the document of carriage` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Article 27. Death of the person liable`

@ref "Convention, Article 27"
GIVEN `the person liable has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action for damages lies against those legally representing the estate` IF
    `the person liable has died`

§§ `Article 28. Jurisdiction`

@ref "Convention, Article 28(1)"
GIVEN j IS A `Jurisdiction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is one before which an action for damages may be brought` IF
        j's `the court is in the territory of one of the High Contracting Parties`
    AND (   j's `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier is ordinarily resident`
         OR j's `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier has his principal place of business`
         OR j's `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier has an establishment by which the contract has been made`
         OR j's `the court has jurisdiction at the place of destination`)

-- 28(2): questions of procedure are governed by the law of the court seised of the case: a
-- reference to another law, inert.

§§ `Article 29. Time for bringing an action`

-- 29(1): the right to damages is extinguished if an action is not brought within two years,
-- reckoned from the date of arrival at the destination, or from the date on which the aircraft
-- ought to have arrived, or from the date on which the carriage stopped.  Which of the three
-- applies follows from how the carriage ended.  29(2): the method of calculating the period
-- is determined by the law of the court seised of the case; the rule counts two years by the
-- anniversary date (NOTES.md fork F6).

@ref "Convention, Article 29(1)"
GIVEN e IS A `Carriage End`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date from which the two years run` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the aircraft arrived at the destination` d THEN d
    WHEN `the aircraft did not arrive` d THEN d
    WHEN `the carriage stopped` d THEN d

@ref "Convention, Article 29(1) and (2)"
GIVEN e IS A `Carriage End`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for bringing the action` MEANS
    `add months` (`the date from which the two years run` e) 24

@ref "Convention, Article 29(1)"
GIVEN l IS A `Limitation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right to damages is extinguished` IF
    l's `the date the action is brought` GREATER THAN `the last day for bringing the action` (l's `how the carriage ended`)

§§ `Article 30. Successive carriers`

@ref "Convention, Article 30(1)"
GIVEN s IS A `Successive Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is subject to the Convention and is deemed one of the contracting parties for the part of the carriage under his supervision` IF
        s's `the carriage is to be performed by various successive carriers and falls within Article 1(3)`
    AND s's `the carrier accepted passengers, baggage or cargo`

-- 30(2): a passenger or his representative can take action only against the carrier who
-- performed the carriage during which the accident or the delay occurred, unless by express
-- agreement the first carrier assumed liability for the whole journey.  30(3): for baggage or
-- cargo the passenger or consignor may sue the first carrier, the passenger or consignee
-- entitled to delivery may sue the last carrier, and each may sue the carrier who performed the
-- carriage during which the destruction, loss, damage or delay took place.

@ref "Convention, Article 30(2) and (3)"
GIVEN s IS A `Successive Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant may bring the action against the carrier` IF
        `the carrier is subject to the Convention and is deemed one of the contracting parties for the part of the carriage under his supervision` s
    AND (CONSIDER s's `the claim concerns`
         WHEN `a passenger` THEN
                 (CONSIDER s's `position`
                  WHEN `the carrier who performed the carriage during which the accident or the delay occurred` THEN TRUE
                  WHEN `the first carrier` THEN s's `by express agreement the first carrier has assumed liability for the whole journey`
                  OTHERWISE FALSE)
         WHEN `registered baggage` THEN
                 `the baggage or cargo claimant may sue the carrier in that position` s
         WHEN `cargo` THEN
                 `the baggage or cargo claimant may sue the carrier in that position` s)

@ref "Convention, Article 30(3)"
GIVEN s IS A `Successive Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the baggage or cargo claimant may sue the carrier in that position` IF
    CONSIDER s's `position`
    WHEN `the first carrier` THEN
        (CONSIDER s's `claimant`
         WHEN `the passenger or the passenger's representative` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the consignor` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the consignee who is entitled to delivery` THEN FALSE)
    WHEN `the last carrier` THEN
        (CONSIDER s's `claimant`
         WHEN `the passenger or the passenger's representative` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the consignor` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the consignee who is entitled to delivery` THEN TRUE)
    WHEN `the carrier who performed the carriage during which the destruction, loss, damage or delay took place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the carrier who performed the carriage during which the accident or the delay occurred` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another carrier` THEN FALSE

@ref "Convention, Article 30(3)"
`the carriers in an action for baggage or cargo are jointly and severally liable to the passenger or to the consignor or consignee` MEANS TRUE

-- 30A (Third Schedule): nothing in the Convention prejudices whether a person liable has a
-- right of recourse against any other person: a saving, inert.
